WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,444
CTI collection is the process of gathering information that may answer an intelligence requirement.

2
00:00:06,444 --> 00:00:21,204
Useful sources include internal telemetry, incident reports, malware reports, vulnerability advisories, vendor reporting, government advisories, ISAC or community sharing, open-source reporting, and threat research blogs.

3
00:00:21,204 --> 00:00:28,697
Internal sources are especially valuable because they show what is happening in the organization's own environment.

4
00:00:28,697 --> 00:00:34,466
External sources add broader context, but they must be evaluated before they drive action.

5
00:00:34,466 --> 00:00:37,238
More sources are not automatically better.

6
00:00:37,238 --> 00:00:42,633
Each source has reliability, timeliness, duplication, licensing, and bias issues.

7
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:47,353
A vendor report may be high quality but focused on customers of that vendor.

8
00:00:47,353 --> 00:00:52,074
A public blog may contain useful technical findings but omit uncertainty.

9
00:00:52,074 --> 00:00:55,071
A community share may be timely but incomplete.

10
00:00:55,071 --> 00:01:00,465
A feed may include indicators that are old, reused, or unrelated to the organization.

11
00:01:00,465 --> 00:01:05,186
Source value depends on the requirement and the decision being supported.

12
00:01:05,186 --> 00:01:10,355
Collection discipline means asking what the source can answer and what it cannot.

13
00:01:10,355 --> 00:01:24,067
If the requirement is about exploitation of a specific vulnerability, the analyst may need vulnerability advisories, exploit observations from trusted reporting, internal exposure data, and incident telemetry.

14
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:35,830
If the requirement is about phishing targeting employees, the analyst may need email security logs, reported messages, domain registration context, and relevant campaign reporting.

15
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:38,453
The source set changes with the question.

16
00:01:38,453 --> 00:01:42,124
Source reliability should be recorded in plain language.

17
00:01:42,124 --> 00:01:50,965
An analyst might note that a source is firsthand, secondhand, automated, community-submitted, vendor-curated, or internally observed.

18
00:01:50,965 --> 00:02:00,631
They might also note whether the source usually reports quickly, whether it corrects mistakes, and whether it separates evidence from interpretation.

19
00:02:00,631 --> 00:02:04,452
This does not require a complicated scoring system at first.

20
00:02:04,452 --> 00:02:12,094
It does require enough discipline that another analyst can understand why the source was trusted or treated cautiously.

21
00:02:12,094 --> 00:02:15,691
Processing and handling rules begin during collection.

22
00:02:15,691 --> 00:02:18,463
Some sources have licensing restrictions.

23
00:02:18,463 --> 00:02:22,509
Some shared intelligence has Traffic Light Protocol handling.

24
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:29,178
Some internal data contains personal information, customer data, or sensitive investigation details.

25
00:02:29,178 --> 00:02:35,546
Speed does not remove the obligation to protect sources, respect privacy, and follow sharing rules.

26
00:02:35,546 --> 00:02:40,267
A good CTI process tracks where information came from and how it may be used.

27
00:02:40,267 --> 00:02:43,339
Collection must stay defensive and authorized.

28
00:02:43,339 --> 00:02:50,157
This course does not teach unauthorized access, intrusive collection, evasion, or offensive procedures.

29
00:02:50,157 --> 00:02:59,223
Defensive CTI teams can do strong work using approved telemetry, incident evidence, trusted reporting, community sharing, and open sources.

30
00:02:59,223 --> 00:03:03,644
The quality of collection is not measured by how much data is gathered.

31
00:03:03,644 --> 00:03:11,061
It is measured by whether the collected material can be trusted, handled correctly, and turned into useful analysis.

32
00:03:11,061 --> 00:03:15,107
A practical collection plan should be small enough to maintain.

33
00:03:15,107 --> 00:03:23,124
List the requirement, the sources selected, the reason each source was selected, the handling limits, and the refresh rhythm.

34
00:03:23,124 --> 00:03:27,470
If a source never changes a decision, remove it or lower its priority.

35
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:30,767
Collection discipline is also backlog discipline.
